course: dictionary
lesson: 4827
title: Hurt: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Hurt is a small word with big jobs. It can be a verb, an adjective or a noun, and its meaning changes with the words around it. «I hurt my knee» means you caused pain or injury to your body. «My head hurts» means you feel pain.
explain: «Her words hurt me.» Nothing touched her body here, so hurt must mean that the words made her feel sad or upset. Words can hurt as well as hits. The phrase «hurt feelings» means the same kind of pain, on the inside.
explain: «It won't hurt to ask» uses hurt to mean cause harm or damage. Always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: Hurt can be a verb, an adjective or a noun, so read the whole sentence to find its meaning.
fact: «Hurt» means to cause pain or injury, to feel pain, to make someone sad, or to cause harm.
fact: Useful phrases with hurt are «get hurt», «hurt feelings», «badly hurt» and «it won't hurt to».
fact: «Pain is a warning sign, so take breaks and stop if it hurts.» Your body tells you when to stop.
fact: «You never kick or throw a ball at someone who is not ready, because it hurts and starts fights.» Never hurt other people.
exercise: «I hurt my knee when I fell off the wall.» What does hurt mean here? | To shout loudly | To make someone feel sad | To feel very cold | *To cause pain or injury to a body
exercise: «Her words hurt me.» What does hurt mean here? | *To make someone feel sad or upset | To run away fast | To cause pain to a knee | To break something on purpose
exercise: «It won't hurt to ask.» What does hurt mean here? | To be injured in a fall | To be happy with the answer | *To cause harm or damage | To feel pain in your head
test: «My head hurts, so I need to rest.» What does hurts mean here? | To run away | To make someone sad | *To feel pain | To cause damage
test: Which phrase means someone's feelings were upset? | Get hurt | *Hurt feelings | It won't hurt to | Badly hurt
exam: Jayden says hurt always means pain in the body. Is he right? | Yes, always | *No, hurt can also mean upset feelings | Only in the morning | Only for animals
